CORE
main.cpp
--cpp14
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ one-element caller pack: two arguments: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ two-element caller pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ two-parameter operator\(\) selected: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A pack expansion in a function template body (`count_args<C, Args...>`)
kept one element when the template was instantiated from a caller whose
own pack had one element: the single-element pack substitution of the
body removed every ellipsis, not just those of patterns naming the
substituted pack.  N5008 [temp.variadic]/8-9.
